  "dispatch_instruction": "Use native delegated-task dispatch with shared isolation from this conversation, preserving its recorded workspace. Each repository todo shares one recorded worktree on <slug>/work; all repository children inherit their orchestrator's workspace (task-preparer children on kind=task todos carry no worktree, branch, or base). Use the supplied brief, semantic key, title, role-attempt facts and resolved selection.profile, selection.kind, selection.instance, selection.model, selection.effort and selection.options. Pass the resolved provider/model and provider-native effort/options to native delegation; do not substitute project defaults. Include the role/attempt identity in the child brief and require it to await confirmed instrukt binding before workspace changes, record writes or stamps. Retain the native child/task id (and matching workspace/branch/head evidence for repository todos) for instrukt binding. Follow native completion delivery.",
  "continuation_instruction": "Use native child/task messaging or continuation for the supplied child id. Within an outstanding attempt, relay the bounded follow-up under that role/attempt. For a newly reserved attempt, bind that attempt to the child id through instrukt first, then send its rendered brief to the child's thread (t3_thread_send, keeping the thread's context); the child works the round under the new role/attempt. Continue an idle or finished child through the same native continuation."
